  "id": "724d4759-2e77-50f7-8ad7-cc3b22062e8f",
  "slug": "blueberry-crisp-dirty-soda-recipe-11989480",
  "name": "Blueberry Crisp Dirty Soda",
  "recipe_type": "drink",
  "brief_description": "Chef John's blueberry crisp dirty soda combines the cozy flavors of a homemade blueberry crisp with the fun, fizzy appeal of a dirty soda. It is made with a delicious homemade blueberry syrup infused with toasted oats, walnuts, and cinnamon and garnished with whipped cream.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Toast oatmeal in a saucepan over medium heat until lightly golden brown. Add walnuts and toast for 30 seconds more. Add blueberry juice, sugar, blueberries, and cinnamon stick and bring to a simmer. Reduce heat to medium-low, and simmer for 20 to 25 minutes. Remove from heat and allow sirup to cool for about 15 minutes. Strain through a fine mesh strainer."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Stir in butter extract, and a very small pinch of salt. Transfer into a smaller container, and store in the fridge until needed."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "To make the dirty soda, fill a glass with ice, and pour in 2 ounces of cream soda. Fill the glass the rest of the way with berry sparkling water, or berry soda if you want something sweeter, leaving a half inch unfilled at the top. Pour in 3 to 4 tablespoons of the blueberry syrup, and stir everything with a spoon for a few seconds. Top of the splash of half and half, And a dollop of whipped cream if desired. Garnish with Grape Nuts cereal, or pinch of cinnamon."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 8,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 25,
